# AI DIRECTIVE: FEATURE SELECTION PROCESS
⚠️ CRITICAL SELECTION DIRECTIVE ⚠️

This directive is triggered by the development workflow and guides the selection and preparation of features for implementation.

# Status Update Context
⚠️ IMPORTANT: Status updates ([to-do], [in-progress], [done]) will be handled in a separate phase after:
1. Feature selection is complete
2. Tests are written and failing
3. Implementation is complete
4. Tests are passing
5. User has verified the changes

Do not update statuses until explicitly directed to do so in that phase.

You must follow these steps in order:

1. Locate Feature List
   - Search `.cursor/rules/gameplay/features/` for feature lists
   - Identify the appropriate feature list file
   - Verify it contains features marked with [to-do] or [in-progress]
   - If no feature list is found, stop and ask for guidance

2. Check Active Context
   - Read `.cursor/rules/workflows/feature-implementation/active-working-feature-context.mdc`
   - If a feature is marked [in-progress], select that feature
   - If no [in-progress] feature exists, proceed to step 3

3. Select New Feature
   - Read parent feature list (core-mechanics.mdc)
   - Select first [to-do] feature
   - Create feature-specific rules file in `.cursor/rules/gameplay/features/battle/features/`
   - Note: Status updates will be handled in the implementation phase

4. Create Feature Context
   - Use template from `.cursor/rules/workflows/feature-implementation/feature-implementation-template.mdc`
   - Create new file: `[feature-name]-implementation.mdc`
   - Copy all feature requirements from parent
   - Add implementation-specific directives
   - Mark all sub-features as [to-do]
   - Include reference back to parent file
   - Add AI directive for test writing phase

5. Gather Implementation Context
   - Search `RisingPunk/mobile/src/battle` for related implementation files
   - Document findings in feature rules file
   - If implementation context is unclear, stop and ask questions
   - If context is clear, proceed to step 6

6. Update Active Context
   - Clear previous context in active-working-feature-context.mdc
   - Archive previous context in the Previous Context section
   - Update with new context:
     - Parent document path
     - Selected feature name and status
     - New feature rules file path
     - Current phase (Selection)
     - Timestamp
     - Related implementation files

7. Prepare for Test Writing
   - Reset working context for test writing phase
   - Document feature requirements for test implementation
   - Note parent and child file references for later status updates
   - Create failing test for selected feature

# Feature Selection Rules
- Prioritize [in-progress] features over [to-do]
- Maintain complete context chain
- Document all decisions and findings
- Stop and ask questions if context is unclear
- Clear previous context before updating active context
- Each feature implementation must lead to a failing test
- Use feature implementation template for all new features
- Do not update feature statuses until implementation phase

# Feature Completion Rules
- A feature is marked [done] only when:
  1. All sub-features are marked [done]
  2. All tests are passing
  3. Implementation is complete
  4. Parent file is updated
  5. Active context is cleared
  6. User has verified changes
- When marking a feature [done]:
  1. Update status in parent file (core-mechanics.mdc)
  2. Update status in feature implementation file
  3. Archive feature in implementation history
  4. Clear active context
  5. Select next feature

# Sub-Feature Management
- Each sub-feature must be completed in order
- Sub-features are marked [done] when:
  1. Test is created and passing
  2. Implementation is complete
  3. Parent feature is updated
  4. User has verified changes
- When a sub-feature is [done]:
  1. Move to next sub-feature
  2. Update parent feature status
  3. Update active context 